# Gecko project instructions

The canonical project name is **Gecko Main** and the canonical directory is `gecko_main`. Use these names for all new scripts, documentation, commands, paths, and configuration. Read `AGENTS.md` for the deprecated-name rule.

Read `AGENTS.md` before project work, `GECKO_SYSTEM.md` before resume work, and `docs/tracker-schema.md` before tracker work. `job-scout/tracker_schema.py` is the central runtime map. Read live tab metadata and `Job Scout` headers before each tracker operation; the documented snapshot is never a column-position map. `scripts/daily_report.py` owns the five-date vertical `Daily Tasks` dashboard; `Daily Run` is preserved historical data and receives no future report writes. `Scratch` is unassigned. Do not create or rename tabs implicitly. `python job-scout/scout.py daily-report --dry-run` is console-only. These files are authoritative; this Cursor rule intentionally does not duplicate them.

For every generated resume, use the shared formatter in `scripts/gecko_v2.py`: each employment heading must render on one physical line as `Job Title - Company Name - City, ST` at left, with verified employment dates flush right on that same line. Keep source fields unchanged and fail Word QA on a wrap or overlap.
